schema: concept-lineage
object:
  title: Minimum Viable Node (MVN)
  type: concept-lineage
  short_description: >-
    The smallest real version of a local initiative that actually does
    something for real people — the smallest loop of people coordinating
    value together that can be run with the people already on hand, before
    tokens, treasuries, or on-chain governance enter the picture.
  source_traditions:
    - lean-startup minimum viable product (MVP)
  toolkit_usage: >-
    Framed as the answer to three specific organizer fears — burnout,
    building something nobody wants, and central overreach — and
    operationalized in the article as three load-bearing parts: a
    one-sentence shared purpose, a way to track value, and five to ten
    people who reliably show up.
  adjacent_meanings:
    - minimum viable product (MVP), the lean-startup source concept
  important_distinctions:
    - >-
      "One is a plan. The other is a working node with a sample size of
      two." — the article's own distinction between writing a whitepaper for
      a community currency and actually lending a neighbour a drill in
      exchange for tracked time.
    - >-
      Autonomous yet connected — an MVN is explicitly not isolationist; the
      article distinguishes "belonging to a network" from "being captured
      by one."
  tensions:
    - >-
      Guarding against central overreach (keeping heavy machinery out) vs.
      tapping shared learning from networks like ReFi DAO and Greenpill so
      the node doesn't reinvent every wheel.
  risks_of_flattening: >-
    Treating "minimum viable" as an excuse to skip the hard part (real
    conversations, an actual exchange with real people) rather than as a
    sequencing discipline that defers technology until human coordination
    is actually straining.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/minimum-viable-node.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
